#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
LOOM Solar GIS v0.12.3 RC1 — Atlas exposure release

Preserves the known-good v0.3.10 Android interaction and visualization while moving
physical spatial state and Atlas attributes into a local SQLite store.

SQLite responsibilities
-----------------------
- stable solar-system entity registry
- epoch-tagged heliocentric state vectors (AU / AU-day)
- local ephemeris cache for repeated scene epochs
- osculating-orbit snapshot metadata
- Atlas profiles, mobility attributes, and node relationships

Authority boundary
------------------
JPL Horizons remains instantaneous astronomical state-vector authority on cache miss.
SQLite persists acquired physical state and read-only Atlas data locally.
Python derives orbit/display geometry and emits the scene contract.
Browser draws and interacts; it does not compute orbital mechanics.

The embedded ATLAS_MINI object is bootstrap seed material only. Once a profile exists
in SQLite, startup does not overwrite it; runtime Atlas reads come from the database.

This build reads the locked adjacent CIVSTATE database through a validated,
query-only adapter. It never mutates CIVSTATE or LOOM Navigator campaign state.
"""
